WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.283
Start on the Map tab in Omni IC.

00:00:02.463 --> 00:00:05.812
It gives the command team a shared view of the
department's map.

00:00:05.992 --> 00:00:10.493
Open Map Layers when you need to see which kinds of
information are being displayed.

00:00:10.813 --> 00:00:17.171
The switches let you choose which calls, units,
stations, points of interest, and department layers
you see.

00:00:17.351 --> 00:00:22.343
The count at the top gives you a quick check before
you interpret an empty part of the map.

00:00:22.663 --> 00:00:25.265
Turn off Points of interest to reduce clutter.

00:00:25.445 --> 00:00:28.325
The count drops from six to five active layers.

00:00:28.505 --> 00:00:31.876
Turn it back on when you need to see saved locations
again.

00:00:32.196 --> 00:00:34.948
Open the main menu and choose Custom Maps.

00:00:35.128 --> 00:00:40.483
This takes you from the department map to the site
references your department has made available.

00:00:40.803 --> 00:00:44.600
Under Indoor Maps, open the Community Coordination
Centre.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:47.319
This example is a fictional floor plan.

00:00:47.499 --> 00:00:52.107
In your department, confirm you have the right site
before sharing a room reference.

00:00:52.427 --> 00:00:55.371
The Ground Floor tab shows the plan and room names.

00:00:55.551 --> 00:00:59.049
A search team could use this to agree on a briefing
location.

00:00:59.229 --> 00:01:03.475
A security team could use it to give another shift a
precise handoff point.

00:01:03.795 --> 00:01:07.485
The tabs at the top switch among the saved floor and
data layers.

00:01:07.665 --> 00:01:10.460
Here, the GIS Import tab is selected.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.181
Check the selected tab before describing what the map
shows.

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:17.467
Back on the Custom Maps list, open Search Maps.

00:01:17.647 --> 00:01:19.737
Choose Indoor and search for Briefing.

00:01:19.917 --> 00:01:24.888
The result includes the site and floor, which helps
distinguish rooms with similar names.

00:01:25.208 --> 00:01:27.043
Open the briefing room result.

00:01:27.223 --> 00:01:31.959
IC returns to the matching floor and shows the saved
zone name and description.

00:01:32.139 --> 00:01:34.635
This identifies a place on the floor plan.

00:01:34.815 --> 00:01:36.841
It does not show who is in that room.

00:01:37.161 --> 00:01:40.959
For outdoor coordination, open Weather Alerts from
the menu.

00:01:41.139 --> 00:01:46.301
Use the search box, severity tabs, or sort choices to
find the alert you need.

00:01:46.481 --> 00:01:49.383
These are fictional alerts for a software exercise.

00:01:49.703 --> 00:01:51.175
Select the Severe tab.

00:01:51.355 --> 00:01:54.469
The list now shows only the severe exercise alert.

00:01:54.649 --> 00:01:57.956
Open it to check what area it covers and when it
applies.

00:01:58.276 --> 00:02:02.201
Check the effective time, expiry, affected area, and
sender.

00:02:02.381 --> 00:02:04.621
This example is marked Expired.

00:02:04.801 --> 00:02:14.188
Community outreach teams, wildland contractors, and
industrial response teams can use the same checks
when planning work around changing conditions.
